Z||000004||stsmithgt||03-13-2001||01:29 PM||||It wasn't so bad with a sunny day around 70º  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flameon1.gif">   instead of rain like it was when I started the exploritory disassembly of the console.  I had the console out for over a week glueing it back together here and there while I was waiting for my cable to come in.  Still needs a little more TLC.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">My landlord came by to work on the driveway.  He was probably wondering why I was working on my car instead of mowing the lawn. ooops. I let neighbors enjoy my 2-stroke weed wacker before I mowed on Sunday.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||danny boy||03-13-2001||07:13 PM||||The guy I got my GT from cut the cat.converter open to gut it and then tried just wiring it shut(yeah, that worked).with all the exaust coming out it melted the throttle cable.The wiring harness was also ziptied(melted) to the rear exaust manifold. Gee, why won't the car run? Oh, my point... I changed cables and I didn't have any trouble.You know that plastic heater duct by the pedal comes off right?||||reg||1
